  "_template_syntax_doc": "Three syntaxes: (1) plain EPITHET = no placeholders, appended after comma (e.g., 'the Nightlord'). (2) OBJECT-EPITHET = contains {o} but not {r}, treated as epithet with {o} substituted to original name (e.g., 'of {o} fame' → 'Tibia Mariner, of Tree Sentinel fame'). (3) TEMPLATE = contains {r} (optionally with {o}), replaces the whole name (e.g., 'The Dread Pirate {r}', '{r} née {o}'). Heritage cases (no original name): titles referencing {o} are skipped — the gate hit falls through to non-composed output.",
